  "body": "A 3 degree tapered cut through work from Z0 to Z12 passes the post with guides at Z-5 and Z5. The upper guide is 7 mm below the top surface.\n\nOn main at 3ffe2338f, the post wrote 496 bytes of Generic ISO Wire EDM output. It also posted the control case with the upper guide at Z25.\n\nThe check compares the programmed bottom plane with the guides. It must check the full work height for the cut. A setup origin must put the work and guides in the same coordinate system.\n\nDone means: The normal post refuses the invalid setup before it writes NC. A regression test checks the refusal and a valid guide span. The diagnostic identifies the affected operation and guide limit.\n",
